{"type":"plan","title":"風鈴の願い","logline":"夏休み、京都の祖母の家で静かな風鈴が再び鳴るまでの小さな奇跡","shots":[{"index":1,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Summer day, bright sunlight on the engawa veranda; Yui walks onto the veranda carrying a small bag, Grandma stands by the shoji smiling.","mode":"still","dialogue":"夏休み、ゆいは、京都のおばあちゃんの家に、遊びに来ました。","cites":[1,6]},{"index":2,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Summer day, the old Edo wind chime hangs motionless from the bamboo hook on the engawa, no sound in the gentle breeze.","mode":"still","dialogue":"縁側には、古い江戸風鈴が、ひとつ下がっていますが、もう、音が鳴りません。","cites":[1,5,6]},{"index":3,"shotType":"Over-the-shoulder","description":"Summer day, over Grandma's shoulder as she points to the silent wind chime and tells Yui it was bought with Grandpa.","mode":"still","dialogue":"「おじいちゃんと買った風鈴なの」と、おばあちゃんは、言いました。","cites":[1,6]},{"index":4,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Dusk, lanterns flicker along Gion street; Yui and Grandma in yukata step onto the bustling festival avenue.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"夕方、二人は、浴衣を着て、祇園祭の宵山へ、出かけました。","cites":[3]},{"index":5,"shotType":"Pan","description":"Dusk, camera pans along the lantern-lit stalls, amber glow reflecting on cobblestones; Yui and Grandma gaze at the rows of shops.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"提灯の灯る通りには、屋台が、ずらりと並んでいます。","cites":[3]},{"index":6,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Dusk, close-up of a wind-chime stall; Yui's hand selects a single blue tanzaku strip from a bundle.","mode":"still","dialogue":"風鈴の屋台で、ゆいは、青い短冊を、一枚選びました。","cites":[3,4]},{"index":7,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Night, inside the tatami tea room, low table lit by a paper lantern; Yui sits writing a wish on the blue tanzaku.","mode":"still","dialogue":"夜、家に帰ると、ゆいは、短冊に、願いごとを書きました。","cites":[2,4,6]},{"index":8,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Night, extreme close-up of Yui's brush tracing the characters 「おばあちゃんの風鈴が、また、鳴りますように」 on the strip.","mode":"still","dialogue":"「おばあちゃんの風鈴が、また、鳴りますように」。","cites":[2,4,6]},{"index":9,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Night, back on the engawa veranda; Yui kneels tying the blue tanzaku to the wind chime, a soft night wind stirs the garden, Grandma watches tenderly.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"ゆいが、短冊を風鈴に結ぶと、夜風が、そっと吹きました。","cites":[1,4,5,6]},{"index":10,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Night, the wind chime sways and emits a clear chirin, its glass tubes catching moonlight; the sound rings for the first time in years.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"ちりん。風鈴が、ひさしぶりに、鳴りました。","cites":[1,5,6]},{"index":11,"shotType":"Over-the-shoulder","description":"Night, over Grandma's shoulder in the tea room; she gently wipes a tear and pats Yui's head as the chime's echo fades.","mode":"still","dialogue":"おばあちゃんは、そっと涙をふいて、ゆいの頭を、なでました。","cites":[2,6]}]}
